Geometry/ftt survey + alignment slots for the sTGC
==================================================

Three tables per slot: stgcOnTpc (1 row), stationOnStgc (4), pentOnStation (16).
Row order is what AGML's <Misalign row="N"/> indexes; pentOnStation row =
4*station + pent, pent order A,D,C,B (script/fttQuadConvention.C).

StFttDb composes them as

    AGML placeholder + stgcOnTpc + stationOnStgc[station] + pentOnStation[row]

with the placeholder = (phx[pent], 5.9, zstation) cm, phx = {0,0,-6.5,+6.5},
zstation = {312.342, 329.953, 347.637, 365.422}.  Translations are cm; StFttDb's
X/Y shifts are mm, so t0/t1 are scaled by 10 and t2 adds straight to z.

Slots, Run 22 (Gene's rule: one date per run year, just before the run; the
day-15..20 window is the safe one, and -10 ideal is outside it on purpose):

  -10  20211010.000000  ideal: all identity. The symmetric placeholder AGML
                        started from, before the detector was built.
  -11  20211011.000000  SURVEY: the numbers that were hardcoded in StFttDb as
                        X_shift_Quad*/Y_shift_Quad*/idealPlaneZLocations_Quad*.
                        Survey of the built detector, no alignment folded in.
  -15  20211015.000001  baseline: that survey PLUS the first FST->sTGC alignment
                        (the row comments carry the geo/align split).
  -16  --               the alignment program's lane, iterations in the seconds
                        field. Day -16 00:00:00 stays empty on purpose so an sdt
                        naming only that date falls back to the -15 baseline.
  -20  --               kept free for "ask with this one".

The -11 slot is a whole day wide (nothing is written at -12..-14), so a job can
name it as sdt20211012.000000 without hitting a sub-minute gap.

Why -11 exists at all: the hardcoded numbers are survey, not design, and until
now they lived only in the code -- and only there, since every -15 and later
entry has the survey ADDED to an alignment and cannot be separated from it by a
timestamp. Ideal (all zeros) is up to 48.49 mm and 2.91 mm in z away from them,
~15 strips at the 3.2 mm pitch, so "no DB" and "ideal" are not the same
geometry and the difference is not negligible.

Verify before pushing, end to end through StFttDb, nothing inlined:

    root4star -l -b -q 'script/fttSurveySlotCheck.C(20211012)'   # PASS, 48/48 exact
    root4star -l -b -q 'script/fttSurveySlotCheck.C(20220322)'   # real data, unchanged

BLOCKED on the DB side (re-checked 2026-10-22): Geometry_ftt holds only
fttFobToHV / fttFobToStation / fttHardwareMap, and Geometry_stgc does not exist,
so none of these three tables can be stored yet. Dmitry has to create
stgcOnTpc, stationOnStgc and pentOnStation in Geometry_ftt first. The push macro
is still to be written; StRoot/StFstDbMaker/macro/fstGeometry_db.C is the
template, tag -> (file stamp, beginTime, description) one row per slot.
